@startuml
!include seq-common.iuml
title Sequence 3 - Live push of a change to every client (Feature 2)

box "Client B (already signed in)" #f5f6f8
participant EventListener as EL
participant DashboardController as DC
participant RemoteServices as RS
end box
box "Server" #eef2f7
participant ClientHandler as CH
participant EventChannel as EC
participant QueuedSubscriber as QS
participant EventBus as EB
participant RequestDispatcher as RD
participant EscalationMonitor as EM
end box

== Subscribing, once after sign-in ==
EL -> CH : second socket: Request SUBSCRIBE_EVENTS + token
CH -> EC : open(request, socket, in, out)
EC -> EC : session token valid?
EC --> EL : Response success
EC -> QS : new (queue of 500, writer thread)
EC -> EB : subscribe(QS)
EB -> EB : publish(CLIENTS n) to everyone
note over CH : the worker thread is free again;\nthe socket now belongs to QS

== Any client changes data (e.g. Sequence 2) ==
RD -> EB : publish(ServerEvent CHANGE)
EB -> QS : onEvent(event)
QS -> QS : offer to queue\n(full: drop the oldest, log it)
note right of EB : publish only queues, so it never\nwaits for a slow client
QS -> EL : write ServerEvent [writer thread]
EL -> EL : remember in recent events
EL -> DC : Platform.runLater(onEvent)
DC -> DC : add line to Live activity
DC -> RS : reload incidents, escalation,\nalerts [BackgroundCall]
RS --> DC : results
DC -> DC : refresh tables;\nshow red BREACHED banner if any

== Every 60 seconds ==
EM -> EM : evaluate every open incident\n(under the dispatcher's read lock)
alt escalation state changed\n(e.g. P1 At risk -> Breached)
  EM -> EB : publish(ServerEvent ESCALATION)
  EB -> QS : onEvent(event)
else unchanged
  EM -> EM : publish nothing
end

== Quiet channel ==
QS -> EL : HEARTBEAT after 20 s of silence
note over EL : no data for 60 s, or the socket closes:\nshow "reconnecting", retry every 5 s
@enduml
